# Normalise line endings so the working tree matches what git stores and what CI checks out.
#
# Why this file exists (context/foundation/lessons.md, two entries):
#   * With core.autocrlf=true and no .gitattributes, every file in a Windows working tree is CRLF,
#     so `npx eslint .` reports hundreds of `prettier/prettier` "Delete `␍`" errors and can never
#     exit 0 locally — while CI, which checks out LF, sees none of them.
#   * That gap is what makes people filter lint output instead of reading its exit code. It once
#     hid an ESLint *crash* (exit 2) behind a grep for four commits, and nine real errors with it.
#
# With `eol=lf` the working tree is LF, local and CI agree, and the exit code means what it says.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
